#!/usr/bin/env sh
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Pre-commit hook — runs on every `git commit` before the commit lands. It
# type-checks the whole workspace, formats and lints the staged files, and runs
# the tests affected by the change.
#
# Three gates, fastest first:
#
#   1. `pnpm typecheck` — THREE commands, not one: `turbo run typecheck`
#      (per-package `tsc --noEmit`) plus `-p tsconfig.node.json` and
#      `-p tests/tooling/tsconfig.json`. Touch a script or a tooling file and
#      the per-package pass says nothing about it.
#
#   2. `pnpm exec lint-staged --no-stash` — staged files only, per
#      `lint-staged.config.mjs`:
#        - cspell on the prose + source globs (read-only; mirrors the CI gate
#          but catches typos before the push)
#        - `prettier --write --ignore-path ./.prettierignore` on the formats
#          Prettier owns here — JSON, YAML, CSS, Markdown. NOT JS/TS: those are
#          formatted by ESLint's @stylistic rules, and the two genuinely
#          disagree, so `.prettierignore` keeps them apart.
#        - `eslint --fix --max-warnings=0` on JS/TS
#        - `markdownlint-cli2 --fix` on Markdown
#
#      ⚠ Prettier and markdownlint-cli2 disagree about Markdown formatting, so
#      for `.md`/`.mdx` the two run as one sequential entry with Prettier LAST
#      (see `lint-staged.config.mjs`). Running only one of them by hand before
#      committing is therefore not a sufficient pre-flight — run markdownlint
#      `--fix` first, then Prettier.
#
#   3. `pnpm test:changed` — the fast test tier.
#
# Why `--no-stash`:
#
#   lint-staged's default wraps tasks in a git-stash dance (stash unstaged →
#   run tasks → restore) to protect unstaged work-tree changes. In v15.x that
#   restore can fail subtly when ANY task fails, leaving the index half-staged
#   with no visible error — the operator sees their commit "didn't happen".
#   With `--no-stash`, tasks run directly against the working tree: a failing
#   task leaves its modifications visible and the error on screen.
#
#   ⚠ `--no-stash` also implies `--no-hide-partially-staged`: a file with both
#   staged and unstaged hunks is formatted whole, and if a task rewrites it the
#   unstaged hunks are staged with it. Stage whole files, or set the rest aside
#   yourself, before committing.
#
# Coverage is NOT run here — it lives on the pre-push hook, where the time cost
# is better amortized.
#
# Bypass (emergency only, never for routine commits):
#   git commit --no-verify
#
#   ⚠ A `--no-verify` commit is the one case CI's whole-tree Prettier and cspell
#   steps exist to catch, since lint-staged never saw those files.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

set -e

pnpm typecheck
pnpm exec lint-staged --no-stash
pnpm test:changed
